<p>President Trump signed an executive order on March 31 that directs federal agencies to help create state-by-state lists of confirmed citizens eligible to vote and tells the U.S. Postal Service to send mail ballots only to voters on approved absentee lists. The order also calls for voter ID and proof-of-citizenship measures, along with secure ballot envelopes and unique tracking barcodes for mailed ballots, according to several reports. The move is likely to face immediate court challenges because states, not the White House, largely run elections under the Constitution, though Congress can set some national rules. Supporters cast the order as an election-integrity effort, while critics and voting-rights groups say there is no evidence of widespread voter fraud in U.S. elections and argue the order could unlawfully restrict voting ahead of the November midterm elections.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/it-6mUS34UYBwbqw-x9aa248hMOXLn0ZzVf2ODtA0KiWmwiRjAlGFrigcRNXOeChRIWN5WK1o4RZdYCoT0dirPv6zt2ai2wb1T3Byb3fSakZlLrlN_ePsSATiJ0J0KoExG2AjUG8ZQIBGeZ8cBAtWkktGpPxssAqklH5O1YPpMhZ5_mRdhU' alt='President Donald Trump after signing an executive order on voting rules and federal voter data.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Broader strategy: Reports describe this as President Trump&#x27;s second election-related executive action since returning to office, suggesting the White House is making repeated executive moves on election policy.</li><li>Federal reach: The order would give federal agencies and the U.S. Postal Service a direct role in voter verification and ballot distribution, pushing Washington deeper into election administration.</li><li>Policy scope: Trump said the administration also wants voter ID and proof-of-citizenship requirements, showing the effort goes beyond absentee-ballot rules alone.</li><li>Midterm context: The order arrives before the November 2026 midterm elections, when Republicans will defend narrow congressional majorities, adding political weight to the timing.</li></ul><blockquote>I don’t see how they can challenge it - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: President Trump cast the order as an election-integrity measure and argued it should survive a legal challenge. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/31/trump-order-election-voting-explainer'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Voting rights advocates: Democrats and voting-rights groups said they would fight the order in court and described it as a large-scale voter-suppression effort that exceeds presidential authority. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/mar/31/donald-trump-iran-shutdown-dhs-tsa-ice-immigration-kennedy-center-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Legal critics: Analysts cited in reporting called the order unprecedented, arguing that a president cannot unilaterally create a federal list of eligible voters or dictate absentee-ballot distribution rules that states usually control. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/31/trump-order-election-voting-explainer'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-signs-order-directing-creation-of-national-voter-list-move-sure-to-face-legal-challenges/article70808991.ece'>Trump signs order directing creation of national voter list; move sure to face legal challenges</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1s91pir/trump_signs_a_new_executive_order_on_mail_in/'>Trump signs a new executive order on mail in voting. Experts say he lacks the authority</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-signs-order-on-mail-ballots-escalating-election-overhaul-push'>Trump signs order on mail ballots, escalating election overhaul push</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-signs-order-tightening-us-mail-in-voting-rules/'>Trump signs order tightening US mail-in voting rules</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/31/trump-order-election-voting-explainer'>Trump’s order to limit mail-in voting: does he have the authority?</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-31-0700/voting-rights-and-voter-fraud-trump-signs-executive-order-create-federal-voter-lists'>Trump signs an executive order to create federal voter lists</a> - allsides.com</li></ul>